  "hints": [
    "Brute force: check all pairs i < j with equal values.",
    "For each position, which earlier occurrence of the same value is the best partner?",
    "Remember the last index of each value in a dictionary/hash map; compare with it when you see the value again."
  ],
  "editorial": "**Brute force** `O(n^2)`: all pairs. **Fast:** scan left to right with a map `last[value]`. At index `i`, if `a[i]` was seen before, the closest earlier equal element is `last[a[i]]`, so the candidate distance is `i - last[a[i]]`. Then set `last[a[i]] = i`. Taking the minimum over all candidates is `O(n)` expected. The `-1` case and updating `last` even after a hit are the common mistakes, and a stress test against the brute force finds both quickly.",
  "complexity": {
    "time": "O(n)",
    "space": "O(n)"
  },
